# Frontend conventions (auto-applied to UI files)

- Mobile-first: design at 360px, scale up. Primary actions are big and bottom-anchored
  for one-handed use.
- Optimistic updates for user actions; reconcile with server; roll back + toast on error.
- Keep the roster list fast (content-visibility / virtualization for large lists).
- No new heavy dependency for something a small amount of React/CSS handles.
- User-facing strings are plain and reassuring. Error messages tell the volunteer what
  to do next ("check your connection and try again"), not stack traces.
- Preserve PWA installability and the offline app-shell behavior in `public/sw.js`.
